{"type_of":"article","id":4959933,"title":"What I check when I review an MCP server","description":"An MCP server gives an AI client a callable interface. Reviewing it means following the path from a...","readable_publish_date":"Nov 2","slug":"what-i-check-when-i-review-an-mcp-server-fne","path":"/martinpisacreta/what-i-check-when-i-review-an-mcp-server-fne","url":"https://dev.to/martinpisacreta/what-i-check-when-i-review-an-mcp-server-fne","comments_count":0,"public_reactions_count":0,"collection_id":null,"published_timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:52:13Z","language":"en","subforem_id":1,"ai_disclosure_level":"fully_autonomous","ai_disclosure_label":"Fully Autonomous","positive_reactions_count":0,"cover_image":null,"social_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1200,height=627,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwav1qhka8dxd3212480u.png","canonical_url":"https://dev.to/martinpisacreta/what-i-check-when-i-review-an-mcp-server-fne","created_at":"2026-11-02T02:52:13Z","edited_at":"2026-11-06T02:55:18Z","crossposted_at":null,"published_at":"2026-11-02T02:52:13Z","last_comment_at":"2026-11-02T02:52:13Z","reading_time_minutes":5,"tag_list":"mcp, ai, dotnet, security","tags":["mcp","ai","dotnet","security"],"body_html":"\u003cp\u003eAn MCP server gives an AI client a callable interface. Reviewing it means following the path from a tool description to the code that reads data, changes state, or authorizes a payment. I want the interface to explain that behavior accurately, including what happens when a request fails.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThese examples come from two public projects: textokit-mcp and dotnet-mcp-orders-server. The pinned textokit revision uses JavaScript modules, not TypeScript; the orders server uses C#. This article is a source-based walkthrough. I inspected the referenced code and test definitions; I did not execute their tests for this article.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"1-names-and-input-schemas-must-match-the-implementation\" href=\"#1-names-and-input-schemas-must-match-the-implementation\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  1. Names and input schemas must match the implementation\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI start with the interface exposed to the client. Can a caller distinguish a lookup from a cancellation? Which arguments are required? Does the implementation enforce the constraints advertised by the schema?\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIn textokit-mcp, paid tool names and schemas are derived from the upstream OpenAPI document:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight javascript\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003etextokit_\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e+\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eroute\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ereplace\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sr\"\u003e/-/g\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e_\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight javascript\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003einputSchema\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eleanSchema\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eop\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003erequestBody\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e?.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003econtent\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e?.[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003eapplication/json\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]?.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eschema\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/index.mjs#L104-L120\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: index.mjs, buildTools\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThat transformation deserves attention. The same file removes top-level composition and conditional keywords in \u003ccode\u003eleanSchema\u003c/code\u003e. Its comment says cross-field rules remain upstream. I would therefore check the upstream rejection behavior before claiming that the advertised schema captures every rule. Publishing a schema and validating a request are separate responsibilities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"2-descriptions-should-state-the-actual-boundary\" href=\"#2-descriptions-should-state-the-actual-boundary\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  2. Descriptions should state the actual boundary\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA useful description tells the client what a tool can do and what must already be true. It should avoid implying access, persistence, or authority that the implementation does not provide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe orders server makes its example data explicit:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight csharp\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eMcpServerTool\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"list_orders\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eDescription\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"List the fictional orders in this server's memory.\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003epublic\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOrder\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eListOrders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eorders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eList\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e();\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/src/OrdersMcp/OrderTools.cs#L10-L12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: OrderTools.cs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e“Fictional” and “in this server's memory” are meaningful limits. A reader should not mistake this demonstration for a connection to a production order system. I also compare descriptions with failure paths: wording that promises cancellation would be misleading if the operation still needs an independently recorded approval.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"3-failures-and-timeouts-need-an-understandable-contract\" href=\"#3-failures-and-timeouts-need-an-understandable-contract\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  3. Failures and timeouts need an understandable contract\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI look for explicit failure responses and bounded network waits. A caller needs to distinguish an unsuccessful request from a successful result containing an error-shaped string.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTextokit builds MCP error results with:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight javascript\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kd\"\u003econst\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003efail\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003es\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e({\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e...\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003es\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eisError\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e});\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003eIts payment requests include:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight javascript\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003esignal\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eAbortSignal\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003etimeout\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eTIMEOUT_MS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/index.mjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: index.mjs, requests and handler\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe timeout applies to individual fetch calls. It does not establish a single deadline for the entire payment flow, which can make an initial request and a signed retry. I would also inspect configuration validation and error sanitization: the handler forwards caught exception messages. A timeout response alone cannot establish whether a remote side effect occurred, so retry behavior needs its own review.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"4-secrets-must-stay-out-of-results-and-logs\" href=\"#4-secrets-must-stay-out-of-results-and-logs\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  4. Secrets must stay out of results and logs\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI trace credentials from configuration into signing or authentication, then inspect output paths. That includes startup failures and exception messages, not only successful responses.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTextokit reads its wallet credential from the environment:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight javascript\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kd\"\u003econst\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003erawKey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eprocess\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eenv\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eTEXTOKIT_PRIVATE_KEY\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003eIts startup log is:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight javascript\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003econsole\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eerror\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e`textokit-mcp ready: \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e${\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003epaid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003elength\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e paid tools + \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e${\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003efree\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003elength\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e free; wallet \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e${\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eaccount\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e?\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eaccount\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eaddress\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003enone (free tools only)\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dl\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e; cap \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e${\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eMAX_CENTS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e cents per call`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e);\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/index.mjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: index.mjs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThat log references the public address rather than the private key. This observation does not prove that every dependency or failure path protects secrets. I would still check returned upstream bodies, signing errors, and captured logs with synthetic sentinel credentials. No such execution is claimed here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"5-writes-and-spending-need-authority-outside-model-arguments\" href=\"#5-writes-and-spending-need-authority-outside-model-arguments\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  5. Writes and spending need authority outside model arguments\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor consequential tools, I ask where permission originates and what limits it. An argument saying “approved” is insufficient when the caller can supply that argument itself.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe orders approval store checks an action, an exact order, and an expiration:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight csharp\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eapproval\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003enull\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eapproval\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAction\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"cancel_order\"\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eapproval\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOrderId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eorderId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eapproval\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eExpiresAt\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eDateTimeOffset\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eUtcNow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/src/OrdersMcp/OrderService.cs#L17-L46\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: OrderService.cs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe implementation claims the approval file through a rename and deletes the claimed file afterward. The tool description explicitly says the tool cannot create approvals. Deployment permissions must preserve that separation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTextokit's spending boundary is different: an externally configured wallet and per-call cap authorize automatic payment. It does not provide the orders server's independent, single-use approval workflow. I would document that distinction and review recipient restrictions and cumulative spending separately.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"6-untrusted-inputs-remain-data\" href=\"#6-untrusted-inputs-remain-data\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  6. Untrusted inputs remain data\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTool arguments, retrieved text, and upstream responses should not acquire authority merely because they appear in a conversation. I follow each value into paths, requests, and state changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eBefore using an order ID in an approval filename, the orders implementation applies:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight csharp\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003epublic\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003estatic\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kt\"\u003ebool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eIsSafeId\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kt\"\u003estring\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e!\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kt\"\u003estring\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eIsNullOrEmpty\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eLength\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026lt;=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eAll\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ec\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kt\"\u003echar\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eIsAsciiLetterOrDigit\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ec\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e||\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ec\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sc\"\u003e'-'\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e);\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/src/OrdersMcp/OrderService.cs#L13-L20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: OrderService.cs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThis restricts the filename component; it is not a general prompt-injection defense. The broader review asks whether external content can bypass approval, influence destinations, or become executable instructions. An allowlist at one boundary provides evidence about that boundary only.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"7-tests-should-check-denied-actions-and-unchanged-state\" href=\"#7-tests-should-check-denied-actions-and-unchanged-state\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  7. Tests should check denied actions and unchanged state\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI read assertions before summarizing test coverage. A test name is weaker evidence than a check that an unauthorized operation leaves the original state intact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe orders tests include:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight csharp\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kt\"\u003evar\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebefore\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etools\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eGetOrder\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"ORD-1001\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e);\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kt\"\u003evar\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eerror\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAssert\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eThrows\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026lt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMcpException\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;(()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etools\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eCancelOrder\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"ORD-1001\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e));\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAssert\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eContains\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"No order was changed\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eerror\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMessage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e);\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAssert\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eEqual\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebefore\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etools\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eGetOrder\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\"ORD-1001\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e));\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/tests/OrdersMcp.Tests/UnitTest1.cs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSource: UnitTest1.cs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThat file also defines cases for expired, mismatched, malformed, and consumed approvals. Textokit's \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/test/smoke.mjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003esmoke test\u003c/a\u003e exercises initialization and tool discovery; it does not establish payment correctness or secret protection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA review report should distinguish source observations, executable test definitions, and observed execution results. Each finding needs a concrete consequence, supporting evidence, and a next action that fits the server's actual scope.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want this checklist applied to your server, I offer a fixed-price review in 48 hours on Upwork: \u003ca href=\"https://www.upwork.com/services/product/2116921806127265220\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://www.upwork.com/services/product/2116921806127265220\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","body_markdown":"An MCP server gives an AI client a callable interface. Reviewing it means following the path from a tool description to the code that reads data, changes state, or authorizes a payment. I want the interface to explain that behavior accurately, including what happens when a request fails.\n\nThese examples come from two public projects: textokit-mcp and dotnet-mcp-orders-server. The pinned textokit revision uses JavaScript modules, not TypeScript; the orders server uses C#. This article is a source-based walkthrough. I inspected the referenced code and test definitions; I did not execute their tests for this article.\n\n## 1. Names and input schemas must match the implementation\n\nI start with the interface exposed to the client. Can a caller distinguish a lookup from a cancellation? Which arguments are required? Does the implementation enforce the constraints advertised by the schema?\n\nIn textokit-mcp, paid tool names and schemas are derived from the upstream OpenAPI document:\n\n```javascript\nname: 'textokit_' + route.replace(/-/g, '_'),\n```\n\n```javascript\ninputSchema: leanSchema(op.requestBody?.content?.['application/json']?.schema),\n```\n\n[Source: index.mjs, buildTools](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/index.mjs#L104-L120).\n\nThat transformation deserves attention. The same file removes top-level composition and conditional keywords in `leanSchema`. Its comment says cross-field rules remain upstream. I would therefore check the upstream rejection behavior before claiming that the advertised schema captures every rule. Publishing a schema and validating a request are separate responsibilities.\n\n## 2. Descriptions should state the actual boundary\n\nA useful description tells the client what a tool can do and what must already be true. It should avoid implying access, persistence, or authority that the implementation does not provide.\n\nThe orders server makes its example data explicit:\n\n```csharp\n[McpServerTool(Name = \"list_orders\")]\n[Description(\"List the fictional orders in this server's memory.\")]\npublic Order[] ListOrders() =\u003e orders.List();\n```\n\n[Source: OrderTools.cs](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/src/OrdersMcp/OrderTools.cs#L10-L12).\n\n“Fictional” and “in this server's memory” are meaningful limits. A reader should not mistake this demonstration for a connection to a production order system. I also compare descriptions with failure paths: wording that promises cancellation would be misleading if the operation still needs an independently recorded approval.\n\n## 3. Failures and timeouts need an understandable contract\n\nI look for explicit failure responses and bounded network waits. A caller needs to distinguish an unsuccessful request from a successful result containing an error-shaped string.\n\nTextokit builds MCP error results with:\n\n```javascript\nconst fail = (s) =\u003e ({ ...text(s), isError: true });\n```\n\nIts payment requests include:\n\n```javascript\nsignal: AbortSignal.timeout(TIMEOUT_MS),\n```\n\n[Source: index.mjs, requests and handler](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/index.mjs).\n\nThe timeout applies to individual fetch calls. It does not establish a single deadline for the entire payment flow, which can make an initial request and a signed retry. I would also inspect configuration validation and error sanitization: the handler forwards caught exception messages. A timeout response alone cannot establish whether a remote side effect occurred, so retry behavior needs its own review.\n\n## 4. Secrets must stay out of results and logs\n\nI trace credentials from configuration into signing or authentication, then inspect output paths. That includes startup failures and exception messages, not only successful responses.\n\nTextokit reads its wallet credential from the environment:\n\n```javascript\nconst rawKey = process.env.TEXTOKIT_PRIVATE_KEY;\n```\n\nIts startup log is:\n\n```javascript\nconsole.error(`textokit-mcp ready: ${paid.length} paid tools + ${free.length} free; wallet ${account ? account.address : 'none (free tools only)'}; cap ${MAX_CENTS} cents per call`);\n```\n\n[Source: index.mjs](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/index.mjs).\n\nThat log references the public address rather than the private key. This observation does not prove that every dependency or failure path protects secrets. I would still check returned upstream bodies, signing errors, and captured logs with synthetic sentinel credentials. No such execution is claimed here.\n\n## 5. Writes and spending need authority outside model arguments\n\nFor consequential tools, I ask where permission originates and what limits it. An argument saying “approved” is insufficient when the caller can supply that argument itself.\n\nThe orders approval store checks an action, an exact order, and an expiration:\n\n```csharp\nreturn approval is not null \u0026\u0026\n    approval.Action == \"cancel_order\" \u0026\u0026\n    approval.OrderId == orderId \u0026\u0026\n    approval.ExpiresAt \u003e DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;\n```\n\n[Source: OrderService.cs](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/src/OrdersMcp/OrderService.cs#L17-L46).\n\nThe implementation claims the approval file through a rename and deletes the claimed file afterward. The tool description explicitly says the tool cannot create approvals. Deployment permissions must preserve that separation.\n\nTextokit's spending boundary is different: an externally configured wallet and per-call cap authorize automatic payment. It does not provide the orders server's independent, single-use approval workflow. I would document that distinction and review recipient restrictions and cumulative spending separately.\n\n## 6. Untrusted inputs remain data\n\nTool arguments, retrieved text, and upstream responses should not acquire authority merely because they appear in a conversation. I follow each value into paths, requests, and state changes.\n\nBefore using an order ID in an approval filename, the orders implementation applies:\n\n```csharp\npublic static bool IsSafeId(string id) =\u003e\n    !string.IsNullOrEmpty(id) \u0026\u0026 id.Length \u003c= 64 \u0026\u0026\n    id.All(c =\u003e char.IsAsciiLetterOrDigit(c) || c == '-');\n```\n\n[Source: OrderService.cs](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/src/OrdersMcp/OrderService.cs#L13-L20).\n\nThis restricts the filename component; it is not a general prompt-injection defense. The broader review asks whether external content can bypass approval, influence destinations, or become executable instructions. An allowlist at one boundary provides evidence about that boundary only.\n\n## 7. Tests should check denied actions and unchanged state\n\nI read assertions before summarizing test coverage. A test name is weaker evidence than a check that an unauthorized operation leaves the original state intact.\n\nThe orders tests include:\n\n```csharp\nvar before = tools.GetOrder(\"ORD-1001\");\nvar error = Assert.Throws\u003cMcpException\u003e(() =\u003e tools.CancelOrder(\"ORD-1001\"));\nAssert.Contains(\"No order was changed\", error.Message);\nAssert.Equal(before, tools.GetOrder(\"ORD-1001\"));\n```\n\n[Source: UnitTest1.cs](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/dotnet-mcp-orders-server/blob/85ee9c52a5197e1108ffd48f8a61103fa51943c6/tests/OrdersMcp.Tests/UnitTest1.cs).\n\nThat file also defines cases for expired, mismatched, malformed, and consumed approvals. Textokit's [smoke test](https://github.com/martinPisacreta/textokit-mcp/blob/fa04fb03e39ed3ac3da8f3a04e605749eeaaf3e6/test/smoke.mjs) exercises initialization and tool discovery; it does not establish payment correctness or secret protection.\n\nA review report should distinguish source observations, executable test definitions, and observed execution results. Each finding needs a concrete consequence, supporting evidence, and a next action that fits the server's actual scope.\n\nIf you want this checklist applied to your server, I offer a fixed-price review in 48 hours on Upwork: https://www.upwork.com/services/product/2116921806127265220\n","user":{"name":"Martin Pisacreta","username":"martinpisacreta","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"martinPisacreta","user_id":4195178,"website_url":"https://github.com/martinPisacreta","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F4195178%2F462e0bce-5293-481a-9f56-31fbf8c0c365.jpg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F4195178%2F462e0bce-5293-481a-9f56-31fbf8c0c365.jpg"}}